    "created_at": "2026-11-18T14:31:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T14:31:36Z",
    "body": "Mounting the machine before generation exposes an incompatible original RotaryContour fixture.\nThe fitted axis is Z, but tilthead.mch has only A and B.\nGeneration refuses it: \"Rotary Contour turns the part about (0.000, 0.000, 1.000); TILT-HEAD 5-AXIS states no rotary on that line (its rotaries: A, B)\".\nAn X-axis contour directs the user to Rotary Parallel.\nA synthetic C-axis mill reaches live-tool safety refusals.\nI refuse the successful mounted RotaryContour case for this follow-up because it would require expanding production support or bypassing safety.\nThe test now checks mounted-machine refusal for quarter and oblique turns, for both turned and baked geometry.\nRotaryOffset uses a supported X-axis machine mounted before generation and posting.\nThe new oblique roughing case uses a closed box at zero stock allowance because the spherical-cap fixture was blocked by the gouge check.\nThe existing quarter-turn spherical-cap case remains covered.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
